Cell[TextData[{
 "Therefore, the obtained multivector is indeed the inverse.  The procedure \
presented above was automated by the command ",
 StyleBox["gaInverse[ ]",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", Below it is demonstrated how to use it. A method  how to compute \
determinant norm of MV for algebras of n\[GreaterEqual]7 are given by \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]On determinant, other characteristic polynomial \
coefficients, and inverses in Clifford algebras of arbitrary dimension (May \
2020), Dmitry Shirokov and (with wrong sign) in Helmstetter,Characteristic \
polynomials in Clifford algebras and in more general algebras, Adv. Appl. \
Clifford Algebras29, 30 (2019)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ff5b74b8-850a-4553-816c-fab33faa42ce"]
}, Closed]]
}, Closed]]
}, Open  ]],

